# js-yaml 5.5.0

Unmodified `package/dist/js-yaml.mjs` and `package/LICENSE` from the official
js-yaml 5.5.0 npm package (MIT). The ESM bundle has no external imports.

- Registry: https://registry.npmjs.org/js-yaml/5.5.0
- Archive: https://registry.npmjs.org/js-yaml/-/js-yaml-5.5.0.tgz
- Source tag: https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/tree/5.5.0
- Published source commit: cb62b2dbbaa0b3e7379d83a5d69d8d52d21b6efb
- `js-yaml.mjs` SHA-256: `213470960d9c2ff1d01f9164e5017749bfc383d8a6ebb8683f35c76e8c6d052b`
- `js-yaml.LICENSE` SHA-256: `a07bc24468b9654ce76a547d47a2db282d07733b715db4c73a98bd63961f9550`
- Archive SHA-256: `23cb2e121ad69acd15fc786b7a9265a81eeeaa9f684ee73e717d6ecdbd8b0c90`

Verified against the npm `latest` tag and official source on 2026-11-10; the
archive matched npm's SHA-512 integrity value. Only the ESM bundle and license
are vendored; the optional source map is omitted.

Use `load(input, {schema: JSON_SCHEMA, maxAliases: 0, maxDepth: 16})` for
restricted data parsing. Keep an input-size limit, catch every exception, and
validate output shape and size. `JSON_SCHEMA` still accepts YAML syntax; it
is not an application schema or a resource limit.
